1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Soul Searching in 'Five Easy Pieces' is a
documentary film directed by Greg Carson.

2
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
A video piece featuring director Bob Rafelson and actor Jack Nicholson,
discussing the production of the film "Five Easy Pieces" (1970).

3
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Self, played by Bob Rafelson.

4
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Self, played by Jack Nicholson.

5
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Five Easy Pieces is a 1970 American road drama film directed by Bob Rafelson, written by Rafelson and Carole Eastman
(as Adrien Joyce), and starring Jack Nicholson, Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Lois Smith, and Ralph Waite.

6
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The film tells the story of surly oil rig worker Bobby Dupea (Nicholson), whose rootless
blue-collar existence belies his privileged youth as a piano prodigy.

7
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
When Bobby learns that his father is dying, he travels to his family home in
Washington to visit him, taking along his uncouth girlfriend (Black).

8
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
The film was nominated for four Academy Awards and five Golden Globe Awards, and was inducted into the National Film Registry
of the Library of Congress in 2000, being deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".
